{"id":557570469,"iid":266065,"project_id":278964,"title":"Allow orbit in release note documentation_link","description":"## What does this MR do?\n\nAdds `orbit` to the allow-list of documentation sets that may use an absolute `https://docs.gitlab.com/` link in a release note `documentation_link`, alongside `charts`, `omnibus`, `operator`, `runner`, and `cli`.\n\nOrbit docs are published from `gitlab-org/orbit/knowledge-graph`, not from this repository, so a relative link cannot resolve. Today neither form passes lint:\n\n- `../../../orbit/` fails rumdl with `MD057 Relative link '../../../orbit/' does not exist`.\n- `https://docs.gitlab.com/orbit/` fails Vale with `gitlab_release_notes.DocumentationLink`.\n\nThis repository already links Orbit docs absolutely, for example in `doc/user/duo_agent_platform/context.md`, so Orbit is in the same class as the other external sets.\n\n## Changes\n\n`doc/.vale/gitlab_release_notes/DocumentationLink.yml`:\n\n- Allow-list regex, the `message` text, and the inline comment all gain `orbit`.\n\n## Related\n\nUnblocks !266055, the GitLab Orbit GA release note for 19.5, which currently fails `docs-lint markdown` on this rule.\n\n## Notes for review\n\n- Touching `doc/.vale` makes `lint-doc.sh` lint every doc file instead of only changed files, so the lint job is slower than usual.\n- `19-5-stable-ee` carries the same rule, so this needs to be backported with the 19.5 release note, or that backport fails lint too.\n- Out of scope here: the `documentation_link` row in `doc/development/documentation/release_notes.md` still says \"Don't use `https://`-style links\" with no mention of the existing exception. That drift predates this change, so I left it alone rather than widen the diff.\n\n/cc @eread","state":"merged","created_at":"2026-10-28T23:12:55.992Z","updated_at":"2026-10-28T23:43:11.584Z","merged_by":{"id":2683848,"username":"eread","public_email":"","name":"Evan Read","state":"active","locked":false,"avatar_url":"https://gitlab.com/uploads/-/system/user/avatar/2683848/avatar.png?v=1793229976","web_url":"https://gitlab.com/eread"},"merge_user":{"id":2683848,"username":"eread","public_email":"","name":"Evan Read","state":"active","locked":false,"avatar_url":"https://gitlab.com/uploads/-/system/user/avatar/2683848/avatar.png?v=1793229976","web_url":"https://gitlab.com/eread"},"merged_at":"2026-10-28T23:43:11.732Z","closed_by":null,"closed_at":null,"target_branch":"master","source_branch":"docs-vale-allow-orbit-documentation-link","user_notes_count":5,"upvotes":0,"downvotes":0,"author":{"id":29600956,"username":"thelle","public_email":"","name":"Talia Armato-Helle","state":"active","locked":false,"avatar_url":"https://gitlab.com/uploads/-/system/user/avatar/29600956/avatar.png?v=1793230685","web_url":"https://gitlab.com/thelle","bot":false},"assignees":[{"id":29600956,"username":"thelle","public_email":"","name":"Talia Armato-Helle","state":"active","locked":false,"avatar_url":"https://gitlab.com/uploads/-/system/user/avatar/29600956/avatar.png?v=1793230685","web_url":"https://gitlab.com/thelle"}],"assignee":{"id":29600956,"username":"thelle","public_email":"","name":"Talia Armato-Helle","state":"active","locked":false,"avatar_url":"https://gitlab.com/uploads/-/system/user/avatar/29600956/avatar.png?v=1793230685","web_url":"https://gitlab.com/thelle"},"reviewers":[{"id":2683848,"username":"eread","public_email":"","name":"Evan Read","state":"active","locked":false,"avatar_url":"https://gitlab.com/uploads/-/system/user/avatar/2683848/avatar.png?v=1793229976","web_url":"https://gitlab.com/eread"},{"id":21826781,"username":"GitLabDuo","public_email":null,"name":"GitLab Duo","state":"active","locked":false,"avatar_url":"https://gitlab.com/uploads/-/system/user/avatar/21826781/duo-bot.png?v=1792265836","web_url":"https://gitlab.com/GitLabDuo"}],"source_project_id":278964,"target_project_id":278964,"labels":["Technical Writing","docs-only","documentation","tw-docops","type::maintenance"],"draft":fal